  "notes": "{引|ひ}く is a versatile godan verb with multiple meanings related to pulling, drawing, and subtracting.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive)\n- Pair: none (but contrast with {押|お}す 'to push')\n\nMEANING 1 - PULL/DRAW:\n- ドアを{引|ひ}く: to pull the door\n- {線|せん}を{引|ひ}く: to draw a line\n- {辞書|じしょ}を{引|ひ}く: to look up in a dictionary\n- {注意|ちゅうい}を{引|ひ}く: to draw attention\n\nMEANING 2 - SUBTRACT:\n- 5から3を{引|ひ}く: to subtract 3 from 5\n- {税|ぜい}を{引|ひ}く: to deduct tax\n\nMEANING 3 - CATCH (COLD):\n- {風邪|かぜ}を{引|ひ}く: to catch a cold\n\nNOTE: Different kanji exist: {弾|ひ}く (play instrument), {轢|ひ}く (run over).",
